project/environment-doubleside-lodchanged-reapply: spoint environment maps walked from inside (aim_sillos) force THREE.DoubleSide via EntityLoader _forceDoubleSide (gated _eapp==='environment'). The one-shot DoubleSide at pool-onReady is NOT enough: streaming-gltf ModelPool swaps mesh LOD tiers as the camera moves, and each swapped-in node (instanced path model-pool.js:1113, new-THREE.Mesh-node path :1185) arrives with its baked material defaulting to FrontSide, so interior faces re-cull mid-walk = residual missing tris. FIX: EntityLoader pool-onReady subscribes handle.on('lod-changed', () => _forceDoubleSide(modelPool._entities.get(entityId).root)) so every tier swap re-applies DoubleSide to the CURRENT root. Residual missing/'flipped' tris are pure single-sided culling, NOT flipped winding/normals (geometry fully present). Witnessed live browser-10 inside sillos: 96/96 env meshes DoubleSide, 0 FrontSide, non-env meshes keep FrontSide (env-gated, no regression).